From 44d4952e128689a6b3a726887d9067f9f1076f97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 20:13:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] K2-Horizon/server: fix tool_choice none content leak, bound
 call args, reject bad slot ids

(a) A parsed turn that is legitimately empty (K2: empty reasoning block, then a
tool call that tool_choice none drops) fell back to the raw generated text in
the non-streaming chat/responses/anthropic result, leaking
`</ifm|think_faster>` into content. A result that went through update() now
always uses the parsed message.

(b) The lenient K2 call grammar allowed any number of argument slots per call
(zero_or_more), so the model could loop on one `<ifm|arg_key>` to max_tokens
(Dawn QA fixture 7). Bound it to one slot per parameter.

(c) POST /slots/{id}?action=save|restore|erase wrapped an out-of-range id
around (get_slot_by_id is meant for completions' id_slot), so /slots/99 acted
on slot 99 % n_slots. Reject ids outside [0, n_parallel) with a 400.

Tests: test-chat (arg bound, server result), server test_slot_save.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BidfYiPxg2nUvGVowCgTPK
